  "interpretation": [
    "DQ: learned correction improves collision/timeout followups relative to ordinary task learning, while learned keep avoids the extra trap failure caused by unconditional clearing.",
    "Revised patch: ordinary learning already restores the declared cases. LearnedChoice keeps, ties TaskTD returns and avoids the fifteen address edits made by AlwaysClear.",
    "Successful task outcomes never start diagnosis or candidate-value training. Successful continuations can be return targets of an already failure-triggered candidate experiment.",
